Why Is Demand Increasing?
Advanced chip manufacturing: Smaller features require increasingly precise measurement and inspection.
Yield optimization: Early defect detection helps reduce wasted processing time and materials.
Complex semiconductor architectures: Advanced packaging and increasingly sophisticated chip structures create additional inspection requirements.
Automation and AI: Automated analysis can help process inspection data and identify manufacturing anomalies.
Fab & Technology Pulse: Process Control Becomes More Critical

Semiconductor metrology measures dimensions, film thickness, surface characteristics, and other process parameters. Inspection systems identify defects in wafers, masks, and manufactured structures. These capabilities are important throughout semiconductor fabrication, where an undetected defect can affect subsequent manufacturing stages.

Technology development includes optical inspection, electron-beam inspection, nanoscale measurement, and AI-assisted defect classification. Equipment suppliers must balance sensitivity, throughput, accuracy, and integration with fab process-control systems.

